      { id: "qna-case-staleness-diagnosis-01", level: 3, q: "Your team notices that items removed from the catalog hours ago still show up in search results, and items added this morning never appear at all — even though offline recall benchmarks on the index look fine. Walk me through how you'd diagnose this.", difficulty: "medium" },
      { id: "qna-case-recall-push-01", level: 3, q: "Product tells you retrieval recall needs to go up substantially, but your per-query latency budget is fixed and can't grow. Walk me through the lever you'd pull on an IVF-based index and how you'd reason about whether the tradeoff is worth it.", difficulty: "medium" },
      { id: "qna-case-index-choice-01", level: 3, q: "You're building a new retrieval service for a very large vector catalog, and the hard constraint you're given is that it must fit in a small, fixed RAM budget per serving node. Walk me through how you'd decide between HNSW and IVF-PQ.", difficulty: "medium" },
      { id: "qna-case-pq-artifact-01", level: 3, q: "A retrieval index using product quantization occasionally returns a candidate that isn't quite the true nearest neighbor, yet the overall system still performs fine end-to-end. Explain why that's expected behavior by design, and describe a place in the pipeline where that same behavior would NOT be acceptable.", difficulty: "hard" }
